and scripts/subtree-usage.md. Root reviewed the withdrawal disposition. Historical candidate retained; no activation approval pending; counters/on-demand command remain and parent outcome is open. No code/config/guidance change.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Bounded work under Jörn’s request for supervision and correction of root derailment; no permanent mechanism, config activation, scientific run or paid API.\nnext_step: Assignment reviewed and released.\nSources: docs/codex.md, docs/coordination/README.md, scripts/subtree-usage.md\n\nAudit native telemetry completion accounting\nReproduced and fixed raw SSE polling rows being treated as invalid usage completions and erasing known cache-write0. Raw observations now separate; malformed/partial/unmarked missing usage still diagnosed, raw-only tokens unknown.20 focused tests pass. Recent-root-only whitelist query observed omitted absent fields and29 valid parsed completions with no projection/regression errors. Raw-SSE branch source/fixture verified, not live exercised; native export dedup remains unverified and no live duplicate charging established.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Bounded diagnosis and same-worker repair continuing the selected local resource-attribution outcome; no config/service, native dedup guess, paid call or other project expansion.\nnext_step: Reviewed result retained in usage contract and tests; worker released. Recheck native dedup only if separately selected or new evidence warrants it.\nSources: scripts/coordination-load.py, scripts/test_coordination_load.py, scripts/subtree-usage.md\n\nVerify fresh-agent resource-measurement discovery\nOne isolated read-only consumer found README->coordination guide->usage contract, gave correct commands and interpretations of count-up units, fork ownership, walltime including idle, manual/supervised delivery, quota/billing and coverage limits. It found stale --help prototype status; assigned worker corrected only docstring/help, reviewed with