ight evidence retained in docs/coordination/five-hour-portfolio-prompt.md and five-hour-review-coverage.md. No substantial scientific execution or human acceptance. At orchestration request, a standalone remaining-window adaptation is retained in docs/coordination/remaining-window-thesis-proposal.md: existing broader odd-polygon theorem candidate, variation section, retained certified example, and assembled PDF/insertion patch. Timing and broader-theorem emphasis are not a newly independently reviewed allocation; no production or human acceptance. Jörn rejected the four-worker cap as unsubstantiated. Revised standalone proposal inventories ten content units, three proof/source reviewers, one assembled reader and two delegated integrators (16 workers plus supervising root); compares four/eight/sixteen without claiming measured capacity. Four detailed allocation messages delivered; final artifact-update notification failed transport. No agents or production launched.\nproject: msc-math\nauthorization: User selected task/prompt design and agent value assessment. Bounded preliminary source discovery, design and reviews, including a review-set coverage check and two existing offline public-API fixture tests. No five-hour package, retained producer overwrite, active manuscript change or paid spending authorized/launched.\nnext_step: Four-worker cap withdrawn. Standalone remaining-window proposal now has 16 disjoint roles, supported source/output table, 4/8/16 comparison and delegated mathematical/evidence integration. Orchestration owns sole approval; no substantial execution approved. New timing and 16-role allocation are not independently validated throughput or PASS claims. Final artifact notification failed; use shared server/source fallback. Receiving root ownership remains conditional.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md, docs/coordination/remaining-window-thesis-proposal.md\n\nAttempt the expiring Codex reset at 04:00 Berlin\nRead-only