nce. Candidate preparation is complete; substantial autonomous programme approval remains absent.\nSources: docs/history/symmetric-partner-candidate-2026-10-03/README.md\n\nResolve the regular-heptagon calibration lead\nBounded preliminary analytic argument covers both heptagon normal-triangle shapes and all cyclic orders. Independent check confirmed placements, constants and template completeness. Capacity formula extends to every symmetric heptagon partner, with sharp oriented fourteen-gon equality shape. Agent-derived; human acceptance, novelty and thesis inclusion unselected.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Small preliminary discrimination of the pending programme, not approval of substantial four-agent execution.\nnext_step: Use this exact result to assess further method development; do not count the solved heptagon case as work needing a multi-hour run.\nSources: docs/empirical-viterbo-design/desk/pentagon-arbitrary-partner/heptagon-symmetric-partner.md, docs/empirical-viterbo-design/desk/pentagon-arbitrary-partner/calibration-extension-preliminary.md\n\nUnify symmetric-partner calibration for odd regular factors\nAnalytic calibration for all odd regular n>=5 derived. Nonobtuse templates fit the incircle; obtuse templates use one extreme antipodal placement or a smaller disk. Independent assembled review found no material error. Exact capacity, sharp equality shape and decreasing constants retained. Generalization is not human-accepted, novelty-certified or selected for thesis inclusion.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Bounded preliminary comparison of method scope; no substantial four-agent execution package launched.\nnext_step: Compare attribution and reader-facing method value with selected pentagon presentation; no enumeration is required for this theorem.\nSources: docs/empirical-viterbo-design/desk/pentagon-arbitrary-partner/odd-regular-symmetric-partner.md\n\nCheck local persistence and one exact rational control\nLocal persistence proved around each odd regular factor within fixed genuine-facet polygon class. Independent review checked exact antipodal endpoint identity and finite strict margins. One rational nonregular pentagon calibration certificate gives all ten template covers, capacity=1 for reference product and exact areas/ratio. Independent arithmetic/geometry audit passed. No production solver run, quantified neighborhood, thesis selection or human acceptance.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Small bounded preliminary method/value discrimination and one control certificate; no substantial portfolio execution or paid spending.\nnext_step: Use exact control and unified theorem in further value/reader-route comparison; implementation comparison must account for actual binary64 input and remains unexecuted.\nSources: docs/empirical-viterbo-design/desk/pentagon-arbitrary-partner/local-calibration-stability.md, docs/empirical-viterbo-design/desk/pentagon-arbitrary-partner/rational-calibration-control.md\n\nCorrect the pentagon certificate packet proof route\nPacket README now matches current analytic Chapters 9–10, historical Sage role and Chapter 14 trust-boundary account. Current and retained source paths resolve; certificate and stdout unchanged, no producer rerun.\nproject: reproduction\nauthorization: Small bounded correction of a demonstrated reproduction-routing error during the selected preliminary preparation; no large execution package launched.\nSources: docs/coordination/oct03-alternative-comparison.md\n\nFoundations and finite-capacity proof exposition\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assi