er; presentation and proof acceptance remain open.\nplan_gap: Remaining optional results are unselected; the general zonotope bound remains conjectural/paused.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded statement/evidence/value comparison before any research execution or thesis addition.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nStructure a bounded future mathematical research packet\nThe dated scientific view records F=11/global HKO questions as outside the submission route; project facts distinguish non-generic arbitrary-polytope support from generic smooth-branch results. These are possible future questions, not current theorem obligations or assigned experiments.\nplan_gap: Exact question, owner evidence baseline, useful alternatives and resources have not been selected; recheck source owners before promoting historical open questions.\nproject: research\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a bounded problem-structuring packet; no large proof search, producer or Pro handoff follows automatically.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md, docs/dashboard/thesis.html\n\nConsider a discriminating authoring-workflow trial\nA current-source passage trial may inform authoring value, but local trials cannot certify whole-thesis readiness. Source repairs have independent value and do not depend on this optional mechanism.\nplan_gap: No trial candidate, success criterion, cost or human-review package selected; retrospective writing outcomes are not a general reliable method.\nproject: thesis\nauthorization: Unselected optional work; not a thesis-completion prerequisite or execution authorization.\nnext_step: Select a concrete trial only if it could change the authoring route enough to justify its cost.\nSources: docs/coordination/thesis-work.md, docs/project-facts.md\n\nDefine consequential friction and the stopping judgment\nOpen judgment about what costs matter for actual MSc project work, what constitutes repair success, and when further investment is worthwhile. No numeric target inferred from examples.\nplan_gap: No grounded baseline or agreed distinction between successful repair and justified stopping with unmet goals.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Discuss concrete project consequences and alternative stopping interpretations; this does not block unrelated bounded intake.\nSources: docs/coordination/goal-map.json, AGENTS.md.commentary.md\n\nSpecify a comparison that can reject a candidate mechanism\nCandidate bounded comparison on one source-grounded decision and later correction; fixture, receiving surface, observable outputs and integration owner not selected.\nplan_gap: Existing returns do not establish which discovery/application mechanism is worth deploying or whether an exact case is adequately reconstructable.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: Choose a concrete case and a discriminating result before investing in implementation; include prior negative evidence and opportunity costs.\nSources: docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-interventions.md, docs/coordination/problem-knowledge-probe.md\n\nCompare coordination at one integration boundary\nCandidate interface rehearsal comparing central, peer and bounded-integrator arrangements. No clean retrospective topology comparison or superiority claim available.\nplan_gap: How coordination changes parent-context demands, unresolved obligations and human rescue is not measured.\nproject: project-repair\nauthorization: 3 October authorized bounded brainstorming, source retrieval and information-producing probes. No substantial execution, host configuration change or thesis restart.\nnext_step: If selected, compare handling of concurrent outputs, an unresolved integration obligation and a late correction; avoid three full project lifecycles.\nSources: docs/coordination/README.md, docs/history/process-audit/REPORT.md, docs/coordination/goal-map.json\n\nSelect a version-aware per-thread prompt-composition view\nAccepted handoff from 01a102da-b805-7f72-ae02-ba9842fa80a8; receipt saved at /tmp/msc-math/prompt-view-handoff-receipt.txt; sender receipt is not established. Bounded inspection found native CODEX_ROLLOUT_TRACE_ROOT request bundles in pinned source. Installed activation, complete deferred inventory, provenance and partial/delta reconstruction remain unverified. Design at ~/.codex/artifacts/recurring-data-2026-10-03/prompt-view-design.txt.\nplan_gap: Full runtime capture and freshness/coverage contracts not yet exercised.\nproject: workflows\nauthorization: Receiving inspection/design only. Implementation, environment/config activation, paid capture, build and restart remain unselected; config implications stay with sender.\nnext_step: Locate one existing native bundle or propose a narrowly approved future capture; verify schema and gaps before choosing a renderer.\nSources: docs/codex.md\n\nLocal-maximality proofs and certificate navigation\nOriginal interrupted/returned packet preserved in fe3475b3; its current source/evidence disposition is integrated into the independently reviewed restart candidate. The new reports identify fresh versus inherited checks.\nproject: oct04-candidate\nauthorization: Historical initial-run assignment stopped and preserved in fe3475b3. Current integration/acceptance is owned by the separately authorized restart tasks.\nnext_step: Historical assignment closed; consult the restart integratio